subject: fix(messages): drawer overflow in compact mode + payload scrollability

Two UI issues found via browser testing (attached element evidence:
drawer at left:-160px, pre not scrollable):

1. DRAWER OVERFLOW — the detail drawer was hard-coded w-[800px] + right-0,
   so in any window narrower than 800px it hung off the left edge.
   FIX (src/shared/components/Drawer.js): all width presets now use
   w-[min(Npx,100vw)] so the drawer caps at the viewport width. This is
   strictly better for every drawer consumer (never larger than the
   screen), no other behavior changes.

2. PAYLOAD NOT SCROLLABLE — the pre content grew unbounded because the
   middle flex wrapper lacked min-h-0 and the drawer body is a nested
   scroll container; long payloads pushed the pre past the drawer height
   instead of scrolling internally.
   FIX (messages page FormatTabs): wrapped the <pre> in a
   min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-auto container and gave the pre
   h-full min-h-0 overflow-auto, so the payload scrolls within the
   drawer. Added a Wrap/No-wrap toggle (whitespace-pre-wrap+break-words
   vs whitespace-pre) so long lines can either wrap or horizontally
   scroll.

VERIFICATION (production build, port 20131):
- drawer class now w-[min(800px,100vw)] (hasMinWidthClass=true)
- pre wrapper: "min-h-0 flex-1 overflow-auto", overflow=auto
- pre overflow=auto, scrollable (scrollH 22018 > clientH)
- Wrap toggle present and functional

